 "rules": {
  "a2Rules": {
   "duplicate": "a draft equal (lower case, letters and spaces only) to another CLO of the same course in the development split, or sharing at least 80% of its content stems both ways (Jaccard >= 0.8); its own original statement excluded",
   "escalation": "a CLO-side draft whose leading verb level (BLOOM table, first six words, highest wins) is above the CLO's level as the model gave it (targetBloom) and at or above the PO/EGA level it gave (sourceBloom); ILO-CLO drafts are checked the other way: an ILO draft above its CLO's level",
   "replacement": "a draft keeping under a third of the original statement's content stems is a replacement, not a revision; whether that is right depends on whether the original was off-subject or weak (remedy assessments above)",
   "values": "any draft or explanation that names an EGA or value other than the one mapped, removes a value reference the original had, or proposes changing the EGA, PO or value itself; EGA names: the four official names and the eval-1.1 short form \"Competent Professional\"",
   "scope": "a draft bringing in a competency the course does not teach (by its description) or turning the statement into another discipline's outcome"
  },
  "scoring": "Agreement, false approvals and false rejections exactly as eval/qualityMetrics.js computes them for each arm (strict: single-verdict, not ambiguous; permissive: any accepted verdict; false approval: clear not-aligned judged ALIGNED; false rejection: clear-ALIGNED judged otherwise). An answer a run never verified is reported apart and never counted as agreement or disagreement.",
  "pairingByItem": "For each item, the number of agreeing answers in each arm (0, 1 or 2 of 2): both right (2/2 and 2/2), only A2 right (2/2 and 0/2), only B2 right (0/2 and 2/2), both wrong (0/2 and 0/2), A2 better or B2 better (unequal counts otherwise), equal and partial (1/2 and 1/2). An item with an unverified answer is listed apart.",
  "pairingByAnswer": "Answer level, run r of A2 against run r of B2 (both agree, only A2, only B2, neither). The two arms are independent samples, so pairing run 1 with run 1 is by index only; the item-level table is the primary one.",
  "disputedOutcome": "For each of the 11 items: corrected in both runs (B2 ALIGNED twice), corrected in one run (once), repeated (B2 not ALIGNED in both runs); with B2's label kind (PARTIALLY_ALIGNED or NOT_ALIGNED), its Bloom levels against A2's, its explanation's reason against the A2 cause above, and its recommendation. A B2 ALIGNED is a correction against the PROVISIONAL label only: whether the item is aligned is the faculty policy question A2 raised (multi-part and broad POs, the course-subject rule), never settled by either arm.",
  "newFalseRejection": "A B2 answer on a clear-ALIGNED item outside the 11 that is not ALIGNED (A2 was ALIGNED in both runs on it).",
  "newFalseApproval": "A B2 ALIGNED answer on a clear not-aligned item (A2 had none: 0 of 52).",
  "bothDisagree": "An item where at least one answer of each arm disagrees with the provisional label.",
  "noiseFloor": "A2's own run-to-run label changes (a2Unstable above) are the reference for how much a difference of one answer can come from re-asking alone; a B2 difference confined to one run on such an item is not read as an effect of the wording.",
  "remedyMatch": "Remap candidates (never scored): provisional RETAG is matched by RETAG_OUTCOME; REWRITE and REWRITE OR REMOVE by REWRITE_TEXT; EITHER (faculty) by both. A non-matching remedy, and every RETAG_OUTCOME outside these candidates, is listed for faculty with its explanation; a re-tag is never assumed right because it is a re-tag.",
  "retagChecks": "A RETAG_OUTCOME answer: the validator requires an empty draft; the explanation should say the tag does not fit (regex /\\b(tag|tagged|mapped|mapping|re-?tag|another PO|different PO|another (EGA|attribute)|does not fit|wrong (PO|EGA|outcome))\\b/i), and whether it names a better outcome is recorded. A RETAG on a clear-ALIGNED item is unsupported against the label; on a level-gap item it is compared with the A2 notes (a re-tag keeps the outcome for clo-po-calc-lower-level, d-po-02, clo-po-prog-lower-level, d-po-08).",
  "unsupportedRecommendations": "The harness count (quality.recommendations.unsupported: a rewrite for a clear-ALIGNED item, a rewrite where a re-tag is expected, a draft held back by the static review, contract refusals), plus every RETAG_OUTCOME for a clear-ALIGNED item and every RETAG_OUTCOME where the provisional remedy is REWRITE.",
  "draftRules": "Duplicate, escalation, replacement, values and scope exactly as A2 (a2Rules), with the same BLOOM table and CLO pool, applied to every B2 draft; then the developer reads every B2 draft as in A2 section 6. The same rules are re-applied to A2's drafts from p2-a2-cases.json so the two arms are counted the same way.",
  "labelExplanation": "Post hoc in A2, pre-registered here for both arms: NOT_ALIGNED on an ILO-CLO pair whose explanation says /smaller (prerequisite )?step|builds toward|does not claim more|same subject/i, and ALIGNED with /\\b(missing|lacks?|no |not |omits|gap)/i; each hit is read by hand before it is reported.",
  "iloDirection": "ILO-CLO: an ALIGNED answer whose ILO level is above its CLO's breaks the level rule (quality.bloom); an ILO draft above its CLO's level, or a draft sharing at least half its words with its own CLO (Jaccard >= 0.5, A2 extra section 3), no longer reads as a smaller step; role_confusion refusals are reported.",
  "facultyReview": "An item needs faculty review when (F1) it is one of the 11; (F2) A2 and B2 labels differ on it in any run, or either arm changed its label between runs; (F3) a B2 answer disagrees with the provisional label; (F4) it is a remap candidate, or B2 re-tags it; (F5) a B2 explanation contradicts its label (read by hand); (F6) a B2 draft is flagged by a draft rule. F1-F3 are academic-relationship disputes; F4 and F6 are recommendation concerns; F5 is a consistency concern.",
  "provisional": "Every expected verdict is developer-written and unreviewed (reviewStatus unreviewed): agreement is with provisional labels, never faculty-validated accuracy, and no difference between the arms is called a model improvement (both arms are the same model)."
 }
}